          {
            "type": "paragraph",
            "text": "Object-Oriented Programming (OOP) is a way of designing and organizing code to make it easier to manage and understand. Imagine you're building a model city with toy blocks. In this city, each building, vehicle, and person is a separate entity that you can design and interact with."
